\subsection{Lab Teams}

<*>
\begin{itemize}
        \item  2-person Lab team (except Lab 1)
        \item  Lab 1 is an individual component which must be done by each person. 
        \item Effective team work is critical to success.
        \item Team ``friction,'' ``tension,'' ``miscommunication,''
        happen to some groups. (5\% --- 10\% of teams).
        \item When these occur, take individual initiative to come
        to TA or Prof. {\it immediately}.
        \item Example problems: ``John isn't showing up for team meetings," \\
        ``Bob and I don't know as much as Jane does and
        she is doing all the work.  I'm worried that the TAs will discover
        this and I will not get a good grade." \\
        ``I'm doing all the work on this team.  Nobody else is contributing."\\
        etc.
        \item {\bf Denial doesn't work:} Don't get stuck by these lame excuses
        for not getting help: ``I don't want to {\it rat} on my teammates."\\
        ``If I wait, maybe the problem will resolve itself."
        \item {\bf You are responsible} for bringing these problems to
        attention of TAs or Prof.
\end{itemize}


<*chn>
Most of the lab work will be done in teams. Pick  out your partner as soon as possible.
We will ask for team lists on the third class meeting.

Working in teams takes attention and effort.
Pay special attention to making sure that your team works well together.
Watch out for the tendency to {\it assume } that everyone is on the
same page.  If your team has problems working together, contact the
instructor or TA's immediately - don't wait. 
We will work with you to get your group on track ({\it done it many times in the past}).

<*>
