\subsection{Lab Evaluations / Demos}


In-person sessions in which you demonstrate correct operation
of your system and answer questions from a member of the ECE474 staff.  
Lab 1 is an individual assignment.    

For subsequent labs (labs 2-4), {\bf both} team members must be present for 
the demo.    


<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}

\subsubsection{Lab Q\&A}  Both team
members must be able to answer a question about  {\it any part }
    the project.  
    
We will expect {\it in-depth} answers from the 
    person who coded/debugged specific parts, 
    and {\it specific though less detailed} answers
    from the other team member.

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
    
\subsubsection{Demos (virtual backup plan in case of UW mandated shutdown)}

Online sessions in which you demonstrate correct operation
of your system.  Lab 1 demo must be interactive and individual as
a 1:1 Zoom with a member of the ECE474 staff.   

For subsequent labs, both team members must be present for demo.  
Online vs Video recorded demo requirements will be announced.
\begin{itemize}
\item {\bf Online: }  A Zoom between both team members and a TA or Prof.  
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Camera must show the Arduino hardware performing lab functions. Video must show the entire hardware system and LEDs or displays.
        \item Audio must transmit required tones from speaker (if applicable). 
    \end{itemize}
\item {\bf Video} Student team will submit a video of no more than 10 minutes
demonstrating all required lab elements. 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Camera must show the Arduino hardware performing lab functions. Video must show the entire hardware system and LEDs or displays.
        \item Audio must transmit required tones from speaker (if applicable).
        \item 
        \item {\bf Pro Tip:} superimpose text on the video listing the lab part
        number during each part of the demo.  (Optional, but TA's will love you).
    \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}


<s>\end{slide}
