\section{Policies}

\subsection{Citing Sources}

In EE474, we expect that you will cite the source for
any information you borrow, quote, paraphrase, copy or otherwise use directly.
{\bf It is an instance of academic misconduct if you fail to do this.}
The UW College of Engineering establishes the procedures and penalties for
Academic Misconduct:

See \href{https://www.engr.washington.edu/current/policies/academic-integrity-misconduct}
    {College of Engineering Academic Misconduct Policy}
      for more information.

I will follow these procedures to the letter if any cases arise
in this class.

Purdue University has a useful tutorial how to understand and avoid plagiarism.

\href{https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/avoiding_plagiarism/index.html}{[ Purdue's plagarism page ]}.


<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}

\subsection{Policies specific our assignments:}
\begin{itemize}
\item Exams in class:\\
      No cooperation, communication, or unauthorized materials.
\item  Exams will be closed book, and closed notes.
\item  You will be able to bring a hand written ``cheat sheet" of notes
to the exam.  The cheat sheet may not contain photocopied material.
\item Lab assignments:\\
      No copying, dictation, or file sharing between lab groups. Any code or
      text included in projects and reports from other sources must have complete
      and clear indication of the source of this code or text.
\end{itemize}

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}

\section{ Grading System, Winter 2022}
\begin{itemize}
        \item ``Flat'' point system.
        \item 450 total points.
        \item Point breakdown is given in the third tab of the 
        \href{https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1pLo5GvlvPP_WHET6sbK7IhZyR_x2ABR-7OutT0kR_mc/edit#gid=870260692}
        {Course Syllabus Sheet} 

        \item Grade will be obtained by dividing your total by 100.
        \item Team members receive same Lab grade (except lab 1).
        \item Each lab's grade is computed based on Demo and Report.
%         \item At end of term, students will rate the lab performance of each team-mate.
        \item In exceptional cases a student's lab grade may be adjusted
              up or down relative to their teammates.
        \item Individual final grades still vary because of performance on 
        individual performance on C-coding assignments, quizes, and exams.\vspace{0.5in}
        
        \item At end of term, at the discretion of the instructor, the class mean
        may be adjusted by adding {\bf or} subtracting an offset from all students in
              the class.  The purpose of this uniform offset adjustment is to ensure
              that the class average properly reflects overall class learning, overcoming
              of special difficulties, and similar factors.
\end{itemize}

  
